to \\infty .$ So, the $y$-axis is the $\\text{unstable}$ line.\n\nTherefore, the equilibrium point (origin) is $\\text{an unstable node (source)}.$ \n\n**Note:** The phase portrait of the system looks as follows:\n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14069185/assets/657508496ddc73c386545152b45cc628d9abddd13ec069daf169d1dc61c1f7be.png)"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186361368 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "24bd917d-c4b3-5bf5-9426-a87a579b03c1" :knowledge-point/title "Classifying Decoupled Systems of Linear Differential Equations"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "5f2cecd1-3a91-5f0d-84db-f2810446da0b" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "stable" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186361370} {:answer/id #uuid "af5f0006-664c-5394-ab72-9b05592a3f7f" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "unstable" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186361371}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "5f2cecd1-3a91-5f0d-84db-f2810446da0b" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "stable" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186361370} :answer-field/id #uuid "d41eadf1-9341-5c41-9d6d-383db0795fca" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/select} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186361369} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "c54c17e7-703b-5f42-948e-4ec9245d7bd4" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "stable" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186361373} {:answer/id #uuid "9e40b134-c909-5fe1-b6f6-44940c3a5cdc" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "unstable" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186361374}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "c54c17e7-703b-5f42-948e-4ec9245d7bd4" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "stable" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186361373} :answer-field/id #uuid "728820dc-4a14-5457-89f8-cf61da910118" :answer-field/key "field-2" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/select} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186361372} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "2b4027e8-1bb8-58df-83bf-be804f07a86e" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "a stable node (sink)" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186361376} {:answer/id #uuid "5ecedba0-c2b1-56d5-b9ca-97565fe130bb" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "a saddle point" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186361377} {:answer/id #uuid "6fdd2ff0-dba3-59ff-8ccd-2fd725e634f6" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "an unstable node (source)" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186361378}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "2b4027e8-1bb8-58df-83bf-be804f07a86e" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "a stable node (sink)" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186361376} :answer-field/id #uuid "7965e926-4dcb-5db4-ab1c-01caf666dc6b" :answer-field/key "field-3" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/select} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186361375}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045463 :db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "d1c82443-160c-5ecb-b7e3-f0a7c6455443" :question/math-academy-id "q-333224" :question/problem "$$\n{\\begin{aligned}{x}^{′}(t)=-2x(t) \\\\ {y}^{′}(t)=-4y(t)\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSelect the correct options below regarding the given decoupled system of linear differential equations.$\\,$\nThe $x$-axis is a {{field-1}} line.\n\n$\\,$\nThe $y$-axis is a {{field-2}} line.\n\n$\\,$\nThe equilibrium point (origin) is {{field-3}}." :question/worked-solution "Writing our system in matrix form, we have\n\n$$\n{x}^{′}(t)=[\\begin{aligned}-2 & 0 \\\\ 0 & -4\\end{aligned}]x(t)\n$$\n\nwhere $x(t)=[\\begin{aligned}x(t) \\\\ y(t)\\end{aligned}].$\n\nRecall that a homogeneous system of linear differential equations has a single equilibrium (fixed point) at the origin.\n\nSince our system is decoupled, its eigenvectors are the following:\n\n- Eigenvalue ${\\lambda }_{1}=-2$ with the eigenvector $[\\begin{aligned}1 \\\\ 0\\end{aligned}].$ The corresponding straight-line solutions of the form\n${c}_{1}{e}^{-2t}[\\begin{aligned}1 \\\\ 0\\end{aligned}]$\nlie on the $x$-axis and approach the origin as $t\\to \\infty .$ So, the $x$-axis is the $\\text{stable}$ line.\n\n- Eigenvalue ${\\lambda }_{2}=-4$ with the eigenvector $[\\begin{aligned}0 \\\\ 1\\end{aligned}].$ The corresponding straight-line solutions of the form\n${c}_{2}{e}^{-4t}[\\begin{aligned}0 \\\\ 1\\end{aligned}]$\nlie on the $y$-axis and also approach the origin as $t\\to \\infty .$ So, the $y$-axis is the $\\text{stable}$ line.\n\nTherefore, the equilibrium point (origin) is $\\text{a stable node (sink)}.$ \n\n**Note:** The phase portrait of the system looks as follows:\n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14069185/assets/062b58a307f6d40c7be59d527cc01d7d301bd3f0115a0074ba0f3dca54412425.png)"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186361379 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "24bd917d-c4b3-5bf5-9426-a87a579b03c1" :knowledge-point/title "Classifying Decoupled Systems of Linear Differential Equations"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "ba18efdf-6d49-547e-95bd-8b5c5d795a3f" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "stable" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186361381} {:answer/id #uuid "c944d4cc-c612-5fdc-aeb4-553d1d434e17" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "unstable" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186361382}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "ba18efdf-6d49-547e-95bd-8b5c5d795a3f" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "stable" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186361381} :answer-field/id #uuid "04fdd5b4-1bad-53f7-aae9-7d1d6f62f3f9" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/select} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186361380} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "aff80473-aedb-5ac9-b7cd-a98e5d623497" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "stable" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186361384} {:answer